---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { NAV_CATEGORIES, SITE } from '../consts';
import { slugify } from '../utils';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="HairMuse is a hairstyle journal for Pinterest lovers — real tutorials, honest tips and saved-worthy hair inspiration."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <span class="kicker">Our story</span>
      <h1>Hi, we&rsquo;re <em style="color:var(--accent)">HairMuse</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A small team of hair-obsessed writers, stylists and serial pin-savers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        HairMuse started the way most hair obsessions do: with a Pinterest board
        titled &ldquo;hair ideas&rdquo; that quietly grew to 4,000 pins. Every time we tried
        one of those gorgeous saved styles, we hit the same wall — the pin looked
        amazing, but there was no tutorial behind it.
      </p>
      <p>
        So we built the blog we wished existed. Every post on HairMuse is a
        real, tested, step-by-step tutorial written for beginners and pros alike.
        No gatekeeping, no &ldquo;just curl it and go&rdquo; — actual steps, actual photos,
        honest notes on what worked and what didn&rsquo;t.
      </p>

      <h2>What you&rsquo;ll find here</h2>
      <ul>
        {
          NAV_CATEGORIES.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`/category/${slugify(c)}/`}>{c}</a> — tested tutorials, from
              five-minute fixes to full looks.
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <h2>Our promise</h2>
      <p>
        Every tutorial is tested on real hair before it&rsquo;s published. If a style
        only works on day-two hair, we&rsquo;ll say so. If it needs three hands, we&rsquo;ll
        warn you. And if a trend is more work than it&rsquo;s worth, you&rsquo;ll hear that
        too.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        Good hair days shouldn&rsquo;t be a mystery reserved for salons and perfect
        genetics. They should be a recipe you can follow.
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Say hello</h2>
      <p>
        The fastest way to reach us is on Pinterest, where we&rsquo;re
        <a href={SITE.pinterest} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{SITE.pinterestHandle}</a>.
        For everything else — collabs, questions, tutorial requests — email
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We read everything.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-band">
      <h2>Join the board</h2>
      <p>
        Follow {SITE.name} on Pinterest for daily hairspiration between posts.
      </p>
      <a class="btn" href={SITE.pinterest} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Follow {SITE.pinterestHandle}
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
